\caption(The disconnected edge participates in cycle detection but contributes no numerical candidate from source zero. Parallel-edge identity and strict ties are checked separately by the same API.)
\alttext(A four-vertex component has negative first edges and two equal total-three routes. Two grey vertices connected by a weight-nine edge have no source path.)

The legacy two-vector result uses predecessor V for both source and
unreachable vertices. The trace additionally uses predecessor-edge E as its
sentinel. A native path record distinguishes unreachable (found=false, empty
arrays, weight −∞) from source (found=true, one vertex, no edges, weight zero).
Recovery checks shapes, source markers, visited parent/edge endpoints, finite
weights and the stored double recurrence. A chain-length guard rejects edited
predecessor cycles without recursion. These local checks do not certify an
arbitrarily edited graph's global acyclicity or optimality, and do not rerun
the topological dynamic program. Results own their edges, arrays and paths.

> Precedence timing: a longest path gives an earliest feasible event time

For nonnegative activity durations on edges, fix the starting milestone time
t(0)=0 and require t(v)≥t(u)+w(u,v) for every precedence edge. Suppose all
milestones are reachable from 0. Following any path gives a lower bound on
t(v), so every feasible timing must satisfy t(v)≥D(v). Conversely, the
longest-path recurrence gives D(v)≥D(u)+w(u,v) for every edge. Thus t=D is
itself feasible and is componentwise earliest. The final milestone time is
a lower bound attained by this precedence-only model.

Use activities 0→1 (3), 0→2 (2), 1→3 (4), 2→3 (8) and 3→4 (1).
Earliest milestone times are (0,3,2,10,11), with binding route 0→2→3→4.
The 1→3 activity can finish at 7, but milestone 3 waits until 10 for the
other prerequisite. The model allows parallel work with unlimited resources;
limited crews, machines, release calendars and uncertain durations would
require additional scheduling constraints.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dag_longest_timing.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<dm::algorithms::WeightedEdge> edges{{0,1,3},{0,2,2},{1,3,4},{2,3,8},{3,4,1}};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::dag_longest_paths_trace(5,edges,0);const auto critical=dm::algorithms::dag_longest_path_to(t,4);
  if(t.result.distance!=std::vector<double>{0,3,2,10,11} || critical.edge_indices!=std::vector<std::size_t>{1,3,4}) return 1;
  std::print("| original activity edge | earliest start | duration | activity can finish | destination milestone | chosen critical route |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :--- |\n");
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();std::vector<double> rows;std::vector<std::string> labels;
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<edges.size();++i) {
    const auto& e=edges[i];const auto u=std::get<0>(e),v=std::get<1>(e);const double start=t.result.distance[u],finish=start+std::get<2>(e),row=4-static_cast<double>(i);
    if(t.result.distance[v]<finish) return 1;
    const bool binding=std::find(critical.edge_indices.begin(),critical.edge_indices.end(),i)!=critical.edge_indices.end();
    std::print("| {} -> {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",u,v,start,std::get<2>(e),finish,t.result.distance[v],binding);
    const auto colour=binding?dm::graphics::RGB{22,163,74}:dm::graphics::RGB{100,116,139};
    plot.line(std::vector<double>{start,finish},std::vector<double>{row,row},"",colour,7)
        .points(std::vector<double>{start,finish},std::vector<double>{row,row},"",colour,4);
    rows.push_back(row);labels.push_back(std::format("{} -> {}",u,v));
  }
  plot.y_ticks(rows,labels).x_limits(-.5,12).y_limits(-.7,5.1)
      .legend({"critical","other"},{{22,163,74},{100,116,139}})
      .title("Earliest precedence-only activity timing; final milestone at 11")
      .x_label("time units").y_label("directed activity").size(1000,560).save_svg("build/dag_longest_timing.svg");
  std::print("\nEarliest milestone times {}; recovered critical vertices {}; project completion {}.\n",t.result.distance,critical.vertices,critical.weight);
}
