\caption(Each segment runs from its tail milestone's earliest time to that activity's possible finish. Its head milestone can occur later because it also waits for other incoming constraints.)
\alttext(Five activity segments show the critical green route taking two, eight and one time units, finishing at eleven. Two grey activities through milestone one finish their branch earlier.)

This is an activity-on-edge interpretation of longest paths, not a new
resource-constrained scheduler. The recovered critical route is one binding
witness. Multiple equal critical routes can exist, just as multiple longest
paths can tie in the previous example.

> Count the actual phases against both vertices and edges

With adjacency lists, complete validation and construction take O(V+E),
Kahn ordering takes O(V+E), and the final pass scans every vertex plus each
edge whose tail is reachable, E_R≤E. Thus the total bound is O(V+E) time
and storage, including owned trace edges and at most E relaxation events.
There is no enumeration of all paths. Recording V topological pops, E
indegree-edge visits and E_R candidate attempts gives V+E+E_R≤2(V+E)
for these recorded phases. Validation, construction and copying are additional
linear work omitted from this particular counter sum.

The reusable forward-band generator connects u→u+d for 1≤d≤b within the
vertex range. It has b(V−b)+b(b−1)/2 edges for b clamped to V−1. Width one
is a chain with V−1 edges; full width is a dense forward DAG with V(V−1)/2
edges. A dense DAG therefore has quadratic work in V even though the bound
is linear in V+E. The generator checks its complete output count and optional
edge cap before allocation; no report-local graph algorithm is required.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dag_longest_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <cmath>
#include <cstdint>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto plot=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();const std::vector<dm::graphics::RGB> colours{{37,99,235},{234,88,12}};
  std::print("| family | vertices | edges | topological pops | topological edge visits | candidate attempts | recorded phase visits | visits / (V+E) |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int family=0;family<2;++family) {
    std::vector<double> sizes,ratios;
    for(std::size_t n:{64,128,256,512}) {
      const auto edges=dm::algorithms::dag_forward_band_edges(n,family?n:1);
      const auto t=dm::algorithms::dag_longest_paths_trace(n,edges,0);
      const auto visits=t.work.topological_pops+t.work.topological_edge_visits+t.work.relaxation_attempts;
      if(t.result.distance.back()!=n-1 || t.work.topological_edge_visits!=edges.size() || t.work.relaxation_attempts!=edges.size() || visits>2*(n+edges.size())) return 1;
      const double ratio=static_cast<double>(visits)/(n+edges.size());sizes.push_back(n);ratios.push_back(ratio);
      std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.6f} |\n",family?"dense":"chain",n,edges.size(),t.work.topological_pops,t.work.topological_edge_visits,t.work.relaxation_attempts,visits,ratio);
    }
    plot.line(sizes,ratios,family?"dense":"chain",colours[family],2.5).points(sizes,ratios,"",colours[family],4);
  }
  plot.line(std::vector<double>{0,550},std::vector<double>{2,2},"",{100,116,139},1)
      .legend({"chain","dense"},colours).title("Recorded phase visits / (V+E) stay below 2")
      .x_label("vertices V").y_label("recorded visits / (V+E)").x_limits(0,550).y_limits(1.35,2.4).size(950,560)
      .save_svg("build/dag_longest_work.svg");
  const double h=std::ldexp(1.0,53);const auto rounded=dm::algorithms::dag_longest_paths_trace(4,{{0,1,h},{0,2,h},{1,3,0},{2,3,1}},0);
  const auto p=dm::algorithms::dag_longest_path_to(rounded,3);const std::uint64_t exact_longer=(std::uint64_t{1}<<53)+1;
  if(p.vertices!=std::vector<std::size_t>{0,1,3} || rounded.result.distance[3]!=h) return 1;
  std::print("\nBinary64 control: stored total {:.0f}; retained route {}; exact integer total of the other route {}.\n",p.weight,p.vertices,exact_longer);
  const double maximum=std::numeric_limits<double>::max();int rejections=0;
  try {dm::algorithms::dag_longest_paths(4,{{2,3,1},{3,2,1}},0);} catch(const std::invalid_argument&) {++rejections;}
  try {dm::algorithms::dag_longest_paths_trace(3,{{0,1,1},{1,2,1}},0,2,0);} catch(const std::length_error&) {++rejections;}
  try {dm::algorithms::dag_longest_paths(3,{{0,1,maximum},{1,2,maximum}},0);} catch(const std::overflow_error&) {++rejections;}
  try {dm::algorithms::dag_longest_paths(3,{{0,1,-maximum},{1,2,-maximum},{0,2,0}},0);} catch(const std::overflow_error&) {++rejections;}
  const auto unreachable=dm::algorithms::dag_longest_paths_trace(4,{{1,2,maximum},{2,3,maximum}},0);
  if(rejections!=4 || unreachable.work.relaxation_attempts!=0) return 1;
  std::print("Unreachable cycle, complete vertex cap, positive overflow and losing negative overflow: {} expected rejections. Unreachable huge-edge candidates evaluated {}.\n",rejections,unreachable.work.relaxation_attempts);
}
